Package: shadowfetch-desktop
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 shadowfetch-themes (= ${binary:Version}),
 shadowfetch-defaults (= ${binary:Version}),
 shadowfetch-branding (= ${binary:Version}),
 shadowfetch-welcome (= ${binary:Version}),
 shadowfetch-creative-base (= ${binary:Version}),
 shadowfetch-fireline (= ${binary:Version}),
 shadowfetch-missions (= ${binary:Version}),
 shadowfetch-drkonqi-pickup (= ${binary:Version}),
# The pillars below were supplied only by live-build/config/package-lists
# (fire-edition.list.chroot). A package list is a build-time seed, not a
# dependency: the ISO had Mission Control, Ember, Firewatch, Phoenix, Fireproof,
# hwscan and the launcher because the chroot was told to install them by name,
# while 'apt install shadowfetch-desktop' anywhere else produced a Plasma
# desktop with none of them and no error. The graph now says what the product
# is, and tools/ship_list_check.py fails if a package list ever again supplies
# a Shadowfetch package this closure does not reach.
#
# shadowfetch-ember is Architecture: amd64 and this metapackage is
# Architecture: all, which is deliberate: the umbra archive is amd64-only
# (repo/conf/distributions), so there is no port for an arch-independent
# desktop to be installable on.
 shadowfetch-control-center (= ${binary:Version}),
 shadowfetch-ember (= ${binary:Version}),
 shadowfetch-firewatchd (= ${binary:Version}),
 shadowfetch-fireproof (= ${binary:Version}),
 shadowfetch-hwscan (= ${binary:Version}),
 shadowfetch-menus (= ${binary:Version}),
 shadowfetch-phoenix (= ${binary:Version}),
 kde-plasma-desktop,
 sddm,
 pipewire,
 pipewire-pulse,
 wireplumber,
 network-manager,
 flatpak,
 plasma-discover-backend-flatpak
Description: Shadowfetch creative workstation (KDE Plasma edition)
 Shadowfetch is a Debian-based Linux distribution for visual artists,
 musicians, and video creators. This metapackage installs the full
 Shadowfetch desktop experience: the KDE Plasma session, the creative-app
 baseline, themes, branding and the welcome tool, and the Shadowfetch
 pillars themselves -- Mission Control, Firebreak and the mission engine,
 Phoenix Recovery, Fireproof updates, Firewatch telemetry, Ember Mode, the
 hardware scanner and the seven-category launcher.

Package: shadowfetch-creative-base
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 krita, inkscape,
 audacity,
 kdenlive,
 ffmpeg,
 fonts-inter
Recommends:
 fonts-jetbrains-mono,
 gimp
Description: Shadowfetch creative app baseline
 Installs the core set of creative applications Shadowfetch users
 expect: 2D, 3D, photo, audio, and video tools. Packages not currently
 available in Debian testing under their expected names (blender, lmms,
 carla, fonts-jetbrains-mono) are listed as Recommends so install
 doesn't fail — Flatpak fallbacks are offered in the welcome wizard.

Package: shadowfetch-nvidia
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 shadowfetch-defaults (= ${binary:Version}),
 dkms,
 mokutil
Description: Shadowfetch NVIDIA setup compatibility package
 Keeps upgrades from the former driver bundle safe without installing a
 driver automatically. Run shadowfetch-gpu to inspect the detected card,
 verify NVIDIA's Debian repository, review the recommended open or closed
 kernel-module flavor, and approve a removal-free driver transaction.
